        "id": "s1_definition",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "What the Haversian system is",
        "marks": 1,
        "why": "The Haversian system is a unit built of several parts, so the answer opens by naming the parts it is about to describe one by one.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Defining only the Haversian canal. The system is the canal plus everything around it.",
          "Writing that it is found in spongy bone. It is found in compact bone."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "One canal, rings around it, cells between the rings, threads joining the cells — that is one osteon.",
        "margin_note": "Name the parts in the definition, then describe them in that order. Four short lines.",
        "mark_note": "Definition",
        "lines": [
          "In compact (dense) bone, a Haversian canal",
          "together with the concentric lamellae, the",
          "lacunae and the canaliculi around it is called",
          "a Haversian system, or osteon.",
          "It is the structural unit of compact bone and",
          "works as a transport system."
        ]
      },
